-- title:
--   At each point place of $w^2=h_\alpha(t)$, the local Kähler differentials are generated by $du$ for some uniformizer $u$
-- statement:
--   Let $m\ge1$ be an integer and $\alpha\in\mathbb C$ with $\alpha\ne\overline\alpha$, and put $h_\alpha(t)=-t(t^m+1)(\alpha t^m+\overline\alpha)\in\mathbb C[t]$. Let $K_\alpha=\mathbb C(t)[W]/(W^2-h_\alpha)$ be the function field of the double cover $w^2=h_\alpha(t)$, where $t$ and $w$ denote the classes of $t$ and $W$; in the setting of the note this is the function field of $V_\alpha$, read in the chart of equation (7) with $w=t(t^m+1)Y$. Let $A_\alpha=\mathbb C[t][W]/(W^2-h_\alpha)$ be its coordinate ring, viewed inside $K_\alpha$. For a point $(c,d)\in\mathbb C^2$ of the cover, $d^2=h_\alpha(c)$, let $\mathfrak m_{(c,d)}\subset A_\alpha$ be the kernel of the evaluation $t\mapsto c$, $w\mapsto d$, and let $\mathcal O_{(c,d)}=(A_\alpha)_{\mathfrak m_{(c,d)}}\subset K_\alpha$ be the local ring at $(c,d)$, the valuation ring of the point place $(c,d)$ of $K_\alpha$; it is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_{(c,d)}\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$. A *uniformizer* is an element of $\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$ generating this maximal ideal. Write $\Omega_{\mathcal O_{(c,d)}/\mathbb C}$ for the $\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$-module of Kähler differentials of the ring $\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$ over $\mathbb C$, and $du$ for the differential there of $u\in\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$.
--
--   For every point $(c,d)\in\mathbb C^2$ with $d^2=h_\alpha(c)$ there exists a uniformizer $u$ of $\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$, that is $\mathfrak m_{(c,d)}\mathcal O_{(c,d)}=u\,\mathcal O_{(c,d)}$, whose differential generates all differentials of the local ring:
--   $$\Omega_{\mathcal O_{(c,d)}/\mathbb C}=\mathcal O_{(c,d)}\,du.$$
--
--   This is the local input for reading off coefficients of differentials at the point places of $K_\alpha$. It belongs to the local study of differentials that the formalization carries out for the genus clause of Lemma 4 of the note (the normalization of $V_\alpha$ has genus $m$).
--
--   **Formalization Note**: the hypotheses $m\ge1$ and $\alpha\ne\overline\alpha$ are `Fact` instances; the condition $|\alpha|=1$ of the note is not assumed. The differentials here are those of the local ring itself, not of $K_\alpha$.
-- source:
--   C. Perassi, Sharp symmetry bounds for real algebraic curves (note): lemma of the formalization, for Lemma 4, pp. 3-4, https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/blob/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/sharp_symmetry_bounds.pdf. Lean: https://github.com/carlok/curve-symmetry-lean/blob/d99bc17a1c397956c05d7417de50f9beed56580f/lean/PlaceDifferentials.lean (C. Perassi)

